{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-005","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"---"},{"kind":"note","ref":"N2","page":1,"quote":"HEAT TREATMENT NOTE:- 1) TO BE HARDENED UPTO 32-35 HRC. 2) THREADS TO BE KEEP SOFT. 3) RETAPPING TO BE DONE AFTER SURFACE TREATMENT AT SUPPLIER END.( IF APPLICABLE )"}],"comment":"The title block heat treatment field is blank ('---') while note N2 specifies hardening to 32-35 HRC and keeping threads soft, but neither defines the manufacturing stage at which hardening applies (e.g., before or after final machining). This ambiguity can cause the machinist to cut hardened material or leave insufficient stock for post-treatment finishing. The designer should fill in the heat treatment field and add the process stage to note N2."
  ,
  "recommended_correction":"Update the title block heat_treatment field with the specified hardness and revise note N2 to state when hardening occurs relative to machining operations."}]}
